   "text": "I read the structure in four pieces and joined them into one SMILES.\n\n**Aryl-pyridazine end.** A 2-hydroxyphenyl group sits on C3 of a pyridazine. C5 of the same pyridazine carries a para-phenylene. The phenylene's other end is bonded to the nitrogen of a piperidine.\n\n**Linker.** The piperidine is substituted at C4 by a carboxamide. That amide nitrogen is bonded to a tert-leucine unit, whose C-terminus is acylated onto a 4-hydroxyproline nitrogen.\n\n**Proline end.** The proline C2 carbonyl forms an amide with the NH of a 1-(4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)phenyl)ethylamine.\n\n**Stereochemistry.** I assigned each centre from the wedges and hashes in the drawing.\n- **tert-Leucine \u03b1-carbon:** the wedged N, the C(=O) below and the tert-butyl at upper right give S.\n- **Hydroxyproline:** the 4-OH is hashed and the C2 carbonyl is wedged. I took this as the standard VHL-ligand (2S,4R) pattern and wrote the chirality tags to match, rather than re-deriving CIP for both ring centres from the picture.\n- **Benzylic carbon:** the wedged methyl, the N at upper right and the aryl at left give S.\n\nI could not run a SMILES parser here. I checked the string by hand, atom by atom, against the drawing.\n\nSMILES: Oc1ccccc1-c1cc(cnn1)-c1ccc(cc1)N1CCC(CC1)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N1C[C@H](O)C[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](C)c1ccc(cc1)-c1scnc1C"
